### dotnet.runtime.js

I am faking the initialization by adding 

```globalThis.__dotnet_runtime_loaded = true;``` to the top of the file. 

I moved the stub replacement which i tracked to be in the function Wc(e) // like i said a lot of tracing... 
and i called it replaceStubs(e) and separated the converters from the Wc function. and called it initConverters, and exposed replaceStubs and bindingsInit

```javascript
export {
  Wc as configureEmscriptenStartup,
  Hc as configureRuntimeStartup,
  Jc as configureWorkerStartup,
  Qc as initializeExports,
  Eo as initializeReplacements,
  ct as passEmscriptenInternals,
  Xc as runtimeList,
  lt as setRuntimeGlobals,
  replaceStubs as __replaceStubs,
  bindingsInit,
};
```


Really all of the changes were to move where things were happening so we can call them on our terms inside index.js, by having them present in export call...

here is the full dotnet.runtime.js https://gist.github.com/HexBlit/296ad395b2d0887ad8ba0f5328fce0c1  gist feel free to use at your discretion.

(honestly, there is enough modifications that I am sure the dotnet team wouldn't exactly like it...)

### index.js 

had to expose the heap views for .NET runtime

in function updateMemoryViews()
```javascript
